    <item>
      <title>gpu_grid_dim</title>
      <link>https://larecs.github.io/larecs/pr-preview/pr-246/larecs/gpu_launch/gpu_grid_dim/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://larecs.github.io/larecs/pr-preview/pr-246/larecs/gpu_launch/gpu_grid_dim/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;p&gt;Mojo function · &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/larecs/larecs/blob/719a3b2f194706458765a85f28510482d015f287/src/larecs/gpu_launch.mojo#L18&#34;&gt;Source&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;script lang=&#34;JS&#34;&gt;
function expandAll() {
    var inputs = document.getElementsByTagName(&#39;details&#39;);

    for(var i = 0; i &lt; inputs.length; i++) {
        inputs[i].open = true;
    }
}

function collapseAll() {
    var inputs = document.getElementsByTagName(&#39;details&#39;);

    for(var i = 0; i &lt; inputs.length; i++) {
        inputs[i].open = false;
    }
}
&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;a class=&#34;&#34; onclick=&#34;expandAll()&#34; style=&#34;cursor:pointer;&#34;&gt;Expand&amp;nbsp;all&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;
&lt;a class=&#34;&#34; onclick=&#34;collapseAll()&#34; style=&#34;cursor:pointer;&#34;&gt;Collapse&amp;nbsp;all&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Returns the number of blocks to launch for &lt;code&gt;length&lt;/code&gt; matching rows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;hextra-code-block hx-relative hx-mt-6 first:hx-mt-0 hx-group/code&#34;&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-mojo&#34; data-lang=&#34;mojo&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;k&#34;&gt;def&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nf&#34;&gt;gpu_grid_dim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;Int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;max_grid_dim&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;Int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;Int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx-opacity-0 hx-transition group-hover/code:hx-opacity-100 hx-flex hx-gap-1 hx-absolute hx-m-[11px] hx-right-0 hx-top-0&#34;&gt;
  &lt;button
    class=&#34;hextra-code-copy-btn hx-group/copybtn hx-transition-all active:hx-opacity-50 hx-bg-primary-700/5 hx-border hx-border-black/5 hx-text-gray-600 hover:hx-text-gray-900 hx-rounded-md hx-p-1.5 dark:hx-bg-primary-300/10 dark:hx-border-white/10 dark:hx-text-gray-400 dark:hover:hx-text-gray-50&#34;
    title=&#34;Copy code&#34;
  &gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;copy-icon group-[.copied]/copybtn:hx-hidden hx-pointer-events-none hx-h-4 hx-w-4&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;success-icon hx-hidden group-[.copied]/copybtn:hx-block hx-pointer-events-none hx-h-4 hx-w-4&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Launches one thread per row, but never more blocks than
&lt;code&gt;max_grid_dim&lt;/code&gt;. Above that cap, the threads of the launch cover the
remaining rows through the grid-stride loop of &lt;code&gt;EntityAccessorIterator&lt;/code&gt;,
so the grid stays at roughly one wave of blocks instead of scheduling a
block per &lt;code&gt;BLOCK_SIZE&lt;/code&gt; rows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Args:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;length&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;Int&lt;/code&gt;): The number of rows the kernel processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;max_grid_dim&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;Int&lt;/code&gt;): The maximum number of blocks to launch. A value
below &lt;code&gt;1&lt;/code&gt; disables the cap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Returns:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Int&lt;/code&gt;: The grid dimension; &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt; if &lt;code&gt;length&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>max_resident_blocks</title>
      <link>https://larecs.github.io/larecs/pr-preview/pr-246/larecs/gpu_launch/max_resident_blocks/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://larecs.github.io/larecs/pr-preview/pr-246/larecs/gpu_launch/max_resident_blocks/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;p&gt;Mojo function · &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/larecs/larecs/blob/719a3b2f194706458765a85f28510482d015f287/src/larecs/gpu_launch.mojo#L41&#34;&gt;Source&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;script lang=&#34;JS&#34;&gt;
function expandAll() {
    var inputs = document.getElementsByTagName(&#39;details&#39;);

    for(var i = 0; i &lt; inputs.length; i++) {
        inputs[i].open = true;
    }
}

function collapseAll() {
    var inputs = document.getElementsByTagName(&#39;details&#39;);

    for(var i = 0; i &lt; inputs.length; i++) {
        inputs[i].open = false;
    }
}
&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;a class=&#34;&#34; onclick=&#34;expandAll()&#34; style=&#34;cursor:pointer;&#34;&gt;Expand&amp;nbsp;all&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;
&lt;a class=&#34;&#34; onclick=&#34;collapseAll()&#34; style=&#34;cursor:pointer;&#34;&gt;Collapse&amp;nbsp;all&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Returns a thread-based upper bound on resident &lt;code&gt;BLOCK_SIZE&lt;/code&gt; blocks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;hextra-code-block hx-relative hx-mt-6 first:hx-mt-0 hx-group/code&#34;&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-mojo&#34; data-lang=&#34;mojo&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;k&#34;&gt;def&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nf&#34;&gt;max_resident_blocks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;device_context&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;DeviceContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nb&#34;&gt;Int&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx-opacity-0 hx-transition group-hover/code:hx-opacity-100 hx-flex hx-gap-1 hx-absolute hx-m-[11px] hx-right-0 hx-top-0&#34;&gt;
  &lt;button
    class=&#34;hextra-code-copy-btn hx-group/copybtn hx-transition-all active:hx-opacity-50 hx-bg-primary-700/5 hx-border hx-border-black/5 hx-text-gray-600 hover:hx-text-gray-900 hx-rounded-md hx-p-1.5 dark:hx-bg-primary-300/10 dark:hx-border-white/10 dark:hx-text-gray-400 dark:hover:hx-text-gray-50&#34;
    title=&#34;Copy code&#34;
  &gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;copy-icon group-[.copied]/copybtn:hx-hidden hx-pointer-events-none hx-h-4 hx-w-4&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;success-icon hx-hidden group-[.copied]/copybtn:hx-block hx-pointer-events-none hx-h-4 hx-w-4&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the number of multiprocessors times the number of blocks of
&lt;code&gt;BLOCK_SIZE&lt;/code&gt; threads each one&amp;rsquo;s thread limit allows, i.e. at most one
full wave. A kernel&amp;rsquo;s register and shared-memory use can make fewer
blocks resident at once; this bound does not account for them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Args:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;device_context&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;DeviceContext&lt;/code&gt;): The device to query.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Returns:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Int&lt;/code&gt;: The upper bound on resident blocks, or &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt; if the device does not
report the required attributes.&lt;/p&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
